@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/belief#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix onboarding: <http://example.org/orexis/onboarding#> .

<> a onboarding:RequirementGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHAT A WORLD MUST STATE OF belief's WORDS, held by onboarding alone before anything is granted
#  (knowledge/domain/onboarding/requirement.md, #838). No agent loads this graph: its kind is
#  onboarding's, and the boot passes over it as it passes over a world's hardware.

#  A BUDGET IS ONE WHOLE NUMBER ABOVE NOUGHT, on whichever role states it: a domain's role beneath the
#  deliberator may, so the shape targets what states the figure. The deliberator reads it as it is made
#  and judges nothing of it, this being where it is judged; that two roles do not state two is onboarding's
#  own requirement, of every package's figures.
[] a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf :budget ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :budget ; sh:datatype xsd:integer ; sh:maxCount 1 ; sh:minExclusive 0 ;
                  sh:message "a deliberator's budget is one whole number of rule executions above nought" ] .
